        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space with inner product linear in its first argument ([[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]]). Write $\\mathcal B(H)$ for the bounded linear operators on $H$ ([[def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators]]); for $M\\in\\mathcal B(H)$, $M^*$ is its Hilbert adjoint, characterized by $\\langle Mx,y\\rangle=\\langle x,M^*y\\rangle$ ([[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]).\n\nA **finite bounded Kraus instrument datum** on $H$ consists of an integer $m\\ge1$, integers $q_a\\ge0$ for $a=1,\\ldots,m$, and bounded operators $M_{a,r}\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ for $r=1,\\ldots,q_a$. It is **normalized** when\n\n$$\\sum_{a=1}^{m}\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r}=I_H.$$\n\nEmpty inner sums are zero. For each outcome $a$, define its outcome operator and operation by\n\n$$E_a:=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r},\\qquad \\mathcal J_a(X):=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*\\quad(X\\in\\mathcal B(H)).$$\n\nThese formulas take values in $\\mathcal B(H)$: each composition is bounded since $\\|M_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*x\\|\\le\\|M_{a,r}\\|\\,\\|X\\|\\,\\|M_{a,r}^*\\|\\,\\|x\\|$, and the sums are finite. This definition specifies only the displayed finite Kraus form; it is not a representation theorem for arbitrary instruments and does not assert that an apparatus realizes these data.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "J. Watrous, The Theory of Quantum Information (Cambridge University Press, 2018; author-hosted pre-publication manuscript), §2.3.1 pp. 100–102 and §2.3.2 pp. 111–113",
              "url": "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~watrous/TQI/TQI.2.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "R. B. Griffiths, Notes on Quantum Information Theory, version 30 Jan. 2004, §7 pp. 1–3, equations (7.2)–(7.9)",
              "url": "https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/course/33-658/qit7.pdf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
