        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ carry a normalized finite bounded Kraus instrument datum as defined in [[def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument]], and let $\\rho$ be a density operator on $H$: a self-adjoint positive trace-class operator with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=1$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]], [[def-trace-class-operator]], [[def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator]], [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]). For each outcome $a$, put $p_a:=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho))$. Then each $E_a$ is an effect ($E_a\\ge0$ and $I_H-E_a\\ge0$), each $\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)$ is positive trace class, and\n\n$$p_a=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho))=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_a)\\in[0,1],\\qquad \\sum_{a=1}^{m}p_a=1.$$\n\nThe nonselective output $\\sum_a\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)$ is a density operator. If $p_a>0$, the normalized conditional state $\\rho_a:=\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)/p_a$ is a density operator; when $p_a=0$, this normalized update is undefined. For a unit vector $\\psi\\in H$, the rank-one density operator $\\rho=T_{\\psi,\\psi}$ has outcome probability $p_a=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}\\|M_{a,r}\\psi\\|^2$. These are conditional mathematical identities; they do not assert that an apparatus realizes the instrument or supply a physical measurement postulate.",
        "strategy": "Define the finite bounded Kraus data explicitly, use the trace-norm density expansion and bounded trace cyclicity to prove outcome positivity and normalization, then normalize each positive-trace conditional update.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
